  "reportes.nota.m2.sin-medidas.uno": "{n} static screen missing its width or height",
  "reportes.nota.ot.estimacion.otros": "{estimadas} of the {total} visits in the period are costed at the per-type estimate ({estimado}) and {reales} at their actual cost ({capturado}). That part of the cost —and the margin that comes from it— is an estimate, not a measurement: recording the cost on the work order replaces it.",
  "reportes.nota.ot.estimacion.una-de-varias": "{estimadas} of the {total} visits in the period is costed at the per-type estimate ({estimado}) and {reales} at their actual cost ({capturado}). That part of the cost —and the margin that comes from it— is an estimate, not a measurement: recording the cost on the work order replaces it.",
  "reportes.nota.ot.estimacion.uno": "{estimadas} of {total} visit in the period is costed at the per-type estimate ({estimado}) and {reales} at its actual cost ({capturado}). That part of the cost —and the margin that comes from it— is an estimate, not a measurement: recording the cost on the work order replaces it.",
  "reportes.nota.ot.intro": "The operations cost is built from two sources and they are NOT the same: what each visit actually cost, when someone recorded it on its work order, and an ESTIMATE per order type —the one in Settings— when not. The estimate charges a metalwork job of {caro} the same as one of {barato}.",
  "reportes.nota.ot.reales.otros": "All {total} visits in the period are at their ACTUAL recorded cost ({capturado}): there is no estimate here, the operations cost you see is what was paid.",
  "reportes.nota.ot.reales.uno": "The period’s only visit is at its ACTUAL recorded cost ({capturado}): there is no estimate here, the operations cost you see is what was paid.",
  "reportes.nota.ot.sin-visitas": "There were no visits in this period, so the operations cost is zero because nobody went to any screen, not because it hasn’t been recorded.",
  "reportes.nota.tarifa.intro": "The difference between the published rate and the net is the commercial discount PLUS the agency commission: both are frozen together in the proposal and the data does not separate them by screen.",
  "reportes.nota.tarifa.sin-tarifa.otros": "{sin} of the {total} bookings in the period have no published rate to compare against ({ingreso} of revenue): either they were created in Sales —where the stored price ALREADY IS the list rate— or their price does not match the net their proposal froze. Those rows show a dash, not a zero: a zero would say the whole rate was given away.",
  "reportes.nota.tarifa.sin-tarifa.una-de-varias": "{sin} of the {total} bookings in the period has no published rate to compare against ({ingreso} of revenue): either it was created in Sales —where the stored price ALREADY IS the list rate— or its price does not match the net its proposal froze. Those rows show a dash, not a zero: a zero would say the whole rate was given away.",
  "reportes.nota.tarifa.sin-tarifa.uno": "{sin} of {total} booking in the period has no published rate to compare against ({ingreso} of revenue): either it was created in Sales —where the stored price ALREADY IS the list rate— or its price does not match the net its proposal froze. Those rows show a dash, not a zero: a zero would say the whole rate was given away.",
  "reportes.nota.vendedor.historicas": "{n} from proposals before 2026-09-28, when the proposal’s creator was not yet recorded: that data CANNOT BE RECOVERED —the log stores the proposal’s name, not its identifier— so those sales stay without a sales rep for good",
  "reportes.nota.vendedor.intro": "The difference between the published rate and the net is the commercial discount PLUS the agency commission: both are frozen together in the proposal and the data does not separate them. Not all of it is a discount the sales rep granted.",
  "reportes.nota.vendedor.raya": "Those rows show a dash, not a zero: a zero in “Discount and commission” would claim none was granted.",
